Package: vpn-kill-switch
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Ivan Nikolajtsev <47537294+localhost1982@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: nftables, network-manager, systemd, sudo, python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-nm-1.0, gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1
Recommends: gir1.2-notify-0.7, gnome-session-canberra, gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Homepage: https://github.com/localhost1982/vpn-kill-switch
Description: VPN kill switch for NetworkManager VPN profiles
 An nftables kill switch: while it is on, the internet is reachable only
 through the VPN tunnel; all other outgoing traffic is blocked, so nothing
 leaks if the VPN drops.
 .
 A watchdog keeps the selected VPN profile connected and reconnects it.
 A tray icon shows the state, offers a settings window (VPN profile,
 server list, notifications on VPN drops) and a journal of VPN drops.
 A statistics command, vpn-stats, summarises connection history.
 .
 The kill switch is NOT enabled at install time. Open the tray icon,
 choose Settings, select the VPN profile and turn the kill switch on.
